.\" Man page for opip
.\" vim: ft=man
.TH OPIP 1 "2026-09-05" "1.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opip \- Create and install integrity-backed offline Python wheel bundles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opip
[\fB--data-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB--no-color\fR]
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build, verify, and install offline Python wheel bundles (\.opip) for
sneakernet and air-gapped targets. Bundles include integrity manifests,
lock files, SBOM metadata, and optional Reticulum RSG signatures.
Standalone
.B opip.pyz
runs without a prior pip install. Kits can embed portable CPython for
hosts with no system Python.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS create
Fetch wheels from PyPI and pack them into a bundle.
Supports
.B --proxy
for HTTP/HTTPS/SOCKS5(h) (Tor:
.BR socks5h://127.0.0.1:9050 ).
.SS install
Install a bundle from a local file, rns:// remote, URL, or git source.
Backends:
.BR pip ,
.BR uv ,
.BR manual .
Also
.B --break-system-packages
and
.B --venv .
.SS kit
Build or verify a USB/airgap kit (zipapps, bundle, optional runtime).
.B opip kit create
\fIpackages\fR
.B -o
\fIDIR\fR
[\fB--with-runtime\fR] [\fB--proxy\fR \fIURL\fR]
.SS self-install
Install opip and pip-rns onto PATH without system pip.
.SS verify
Verify bundle integrity, authenticity, and provenance.
.SS export
Copy a verified bundle for offline sharing (includes .rsg sidecar when present).
.SS list
List registered bundles or installed bundle records.
.SS uninstall
Uninstall packages installed from a registered bundle.
.SS update
Rebuild a registered bundle from stored requirements.
.SS keygen
Generate a Reticulum identity for bundle signing.
.SS register-windows
Register .opip file association and Explorer context menus (Windows).
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Bundle a project:
.RS
opip create
.RE
.B Install on an air-gapped machine:
.RS
opip verify my-bundle.opip
.br
opip install my-bundle.opip --venv .venv
.RE
.B USB kit with portable Python:
.RS
opip kit create nomadnet -o /media/usb --with-runtime
.br
/media/usb/install.sh
.RE
.B Run without installing:
.RS
python3 opip.pyz help airgap
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPIP_DATA_DIR
State directory for bundle registry and install records.
.TP
.B OPIP_SIGNER
Default signer identity for verify and install.
.TP
.B OPIP_PROXY
Default proxy for create/kit downloads.
.TP
.B OPIP_BACKEND
Install backend: pip, uv, or manual.
.TP
.B PIP_RNS_CONFIG
Config directory for pip-rns aliases resolved during rns:// installs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pip-rns (1),
.BR pipx-rns (1)
